去给那台老古董上紧发条，
上去跑一把了吗？
So, are you gonna
wind yours up
and give it a shot, then?

264
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:51,640
成绩挺漂亮，
但绝不是不可战胜的。
That's a good time,
but not unbeatable.

265
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:55,600
梅：看来战书已经下给
我们这帮“古董鉴宝队”了。
MAY: So, the gauntlet's
thrown down
for the antique roadshow.

266
00:15:58,280 --> 00:16:02,280
减掉那些重量后……
起步真是一下子窜了出去。
That weight...
It really did leap away.

267
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:04,720
梅：没错，这确实不是斯提格
最帅气逼人的时刻，
MAY: Yes, this isn't the
coolest The Stig
has ever looked,

268
00:16:04,760 --> 00:16:07,920
但这辆希利在他手里，
弯道姿态
相当利落。
but in the Healy he was in
good shape
through the corners.

269
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:15,880
噢，噢！越来越近了！
Oh, oh! Getting close.

270
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:17,880
希利闪电般攻克了最后两个弯角，
The Healey blitzed
the last two turns,

271
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:20,880
但它能打破59秒26吗？
but would it beat 59.26?

272
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:23,680
[欢呼声]
[CHEERING]

273
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:26,320
赢了！大胡子党以一须之差险胜！
Yes, the beards had won it
by a whisker.

274
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:29,800
心服口服。
Fair enough.

275
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:32,280
年纪、阅历、粗花呢，
外加脸上的
那一小撮胡子，
Age, experience, tweed
and a little bit
of facial hair

276
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:34,680
正是赢得爬坡赛
所必需的法宝。
is what it takes to win
at hill climbing.

277
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:37,960
反正我知道自己更想开哪辆回家——
有车顶和挡风玻璃的那辆。
I know which one I'd rather go
home in, the one with a roof
and a windscreen.

278
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:45,000
你敢信？
Can you believe it?

279
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:47,240
算了算了，言归正传。
Anyway, anyway.

280
00:16:47,280 --> 00:16:50,000
我们现在得翻篇了，
因为接下来又到了
请明星……
We must now move on,
because it's time
to put a star

281
00:16:50,040 --> 00:16:52,320
驾驶我们的平价车！
in our reasonably priced car.

282
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:56,240
话说，有迹象表明，
我今晚请来的嘉宾是个同性恋，
Now, there is evidence
to suggest
that my guest tonight is gay,

283
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:59,320
但他坚称自己不是。
就跟理查德·哈蒙德一样。
but he says he isn't.
Much like Richard Hammond.

284
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:03,080
让我们掌声欢迎《小不列颠》的高个子半边天——
大卫·威廉姆斯！
So please welcome the top half
of Little Britain,
David Walliams!

285
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:05,760
谢谢！
Thank you!

286
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:08,120
真是不胜荣幸！
What an honour!

287
00:17:14,040 --> 00:17:15,800
[听不清]
[INAUDIBLE]

288
00:17:18,840 --> 00:17:21,000
要是可以的话，我想先把这事弄弄清楚，
I wanna get this cleared up
right away, if I may,

289
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:23,680
你到底是不是基佬？
you're not actually gay,
are you?

290
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:25,720
-这个嘛，我……
-[笑声]
-Well, I...
-[LAUGHTER]

291
00:17:26,560 --> 00:17:28,200
那得看问的人是谁了！
Depends who's asking!

292
00:17:28,240 --> 00:17:31,720
-我问的。
-那不是，我可不会跟你上床，绝不可能。
-Me.
-Well, no, I wouldn't have sex
with you, no.

293
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:35,520
-[笑声]
-这下清楚了。
你不是基佬。
-[LAUGHTER]
-So that's clear.
You're not gay.

294
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:37,960
顺便声明一下，我也不是基佬。
I'm not gay either,
I'd just like to say there.

295
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,440
好多人都觉得我是，
就因为我不看足球。
A lot of people think I am
because I don't like football.

296
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:42,920
-但你也不看足球，对吧？
-不看。
-But you don't like football
either, do you?
-No.

297
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:45,720
倒也不是讨厌，
我纯粹就是提不起兴趣。
Well, I don't dislike it,
I'm just not really
interested in it.

298
00:17:45,760 --> 00:17:48,760
我总觉得，他们就不能直接决出谁最强，
然后到此为止吗？
I just think, can't they
decide what team is the best
and just leave it there.

299
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:51,160
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

300
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:54,400
非得年复一年一直踢下去，
我真搞不懂。
It seems they have to go on
year by year,
I don't understand.

301
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:58,280
你前几天不是碰到了一个球员，
结果完全不知道人家是谁吗？
Didn't you meet a footballer
the other day and you had
no clue who he was?

302
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:01,360
呃，我能认出他纯粹是因为他老婆
是路易丝·诺丁，
Well, I only knew who he was
because he's married
to Louise Nurding,

303
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,920
以前是“永恒乐团”的成员。
who used to be in Eternal.

304
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:05,600
-杰米·雷德克纳普，对吧？
-[观众附和]
-Jamie Redknapp,
is that right?
-[AUDIENCE AGREES]

305
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:09,920
我当时正开车进……
噢，开车！
咱们这么快就切入开车主题了。
I was driving into...
Ooh, driving!
We're on to driving already.

306
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,800
我当时正开车进停车场，他刚好开车出来。
I was driving into a car park,
and he was coming out.

307
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:13,680
那正好是去年喜剧奖颁奖礼
的第二天晚上，
And it was actually the night
after the Comedy Awards
last year

308
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:17,040
他说：“祝贺你们获奖啊！”
我应道：“噢，谢谢。”
and he said, "Well done
on those awards!"
I went, "Oh, thank you."

309
00:18:17,080 --> 00:18:18,680
然后我都不知道该跟人家回什么，
因为我根本不知道……
And I didn't know
what to say to him.
'cause I didn't know...

310
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:20,480
他还在踢球吗？他在哪支队踢啊？
Did he still play?
What team is he on.

311
00:18:20,520 --> 00:18:23,520
于是我脱口而出一句：
“那个……继续猛踢皮球啊！”
So I just went,
"Well, keep kicking
those balls!"

312
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,960
[观众笑声]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHS]

313
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:29,680
“我怎么就不能像个纯爷们呢？
我怎么连这都不懂？”
"Why can't I be a man?
Why don't I know
these things?"

314
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:32,840
因为《小不列颠》现在
火爆程度简直突破天际了，不是吗？
Because Little Britainnow
is just off the scale,
isn't it?

315
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:36,680
这完全是现象级的成功，剧本写得太绝了。
It's the most phenomenal
success. It's so well written.

316
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:39,160
承蒙夸奖，
平时根本没人提起剧本这茬。
That's kind of you to say,
'cause no one
ever really mentions that.

317
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,760
全是你和马特两个人包办的，对吧？
You and Matt do all of it,
don't you?

318
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:43,200
对，不过其实第三季里，呃，
Yeah, well, actually in the
third series, um,

319
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:46,240
也有另外两位编剧参与供稿，但是……
we had some contributions
from a couple of
other writers, but...

320
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:48,360
还有件事我也注意到了，
就是你现在……
And the other thing as well
I've noticed is that
you can now...

321
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:50,600
在我看来，如今喜剧的尺度
I seems to me you can push the
boundaries of comedy now

322
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:52,400
似乎比以往任何时候都更能放得开。
further than probably
ever before.

323
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:56,480
但奇怪的是，越是大家都坚信
有些话绝不能乱讲，
But it's like the more you get
convinced you can't say
certain things,

324
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:59,680
比如绝不能演什么老太太
一提到黑人就狂吐不止，
you can't have old ladies
vomiting whenever
black people are mentioned,

325
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:01,960
结果节目里偏偏就演老太太
一听到提黑人就大吐特吐。
and then there they are
vomiting whenever black people
are mentioned.

326
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:06,200
呃，那当然是对某些人
种族歧视观念的夸张讽刺，
Well, that is of course
an exaggeration
about people's racist views,

327
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:08,320
但我感觉观众最反感的
其实还真是这段，
but I think that's the one
people dislike the most,
actually,

328
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:10,680
因为我觉得大家单纯只是
不想看见有人在那儿呕吐罢了。
because I think people
actually don't like to see
people vomit.

329
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:13,680
没错。吉米·卡尔也是这种人，
逮着什么都能编成段子。
Yeah. Jimmy Carr is another
one that makes jokes
out of anything.

330
00:19:13,720 --> 00:19:17,200
-他毕竟是个脱口秀演员嘛。
-是啊，他是真能把任何事都拿来开涮。
-He's a comedian, isn't he?
-Yeah. He will make a joke
out of absolutely anything.

331
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:18,880
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

332
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:20,600
-他人呢？
-哦？他现在居然在观众席里？
-Where is he?
-Oh, he's in the audience,
now?

333
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:22,960
在那儿呢，看。
他每周都跑来现场。
He's there, look.
He comes every week.

334
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,880
过来坐这儿，吉米·卡尔，快上来。
Come sit here, Jimmy Carr,
come on.

335
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:27,160
才不是，他刚才紧张得要命，
生怕自己的榜首宝座被刷下来。
No, he was very nervous
that he was gonna be
knocked off the top.

336
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:29,280
总得想办法刷点存在感嘛。
Try and stay involved.

337
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:31,960
既然你都邀他上来了。
女士们先生们，吉米·卡尔来了！
You've invited him up.
Ladies and gentlemen,
Jimmy Carr is here!

338
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,840
[欢呼声]
[CHEERING]

339
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:43,240
你还真是无论什么事都能编成段子，对吧？
You will make a joke
out of anything, won't you?

340
00:19:43,280 --> 00:19:44,680
对，差不多吧，
有何不可呢？
Yeah, pretty much, yeah.
Why not?

341
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:48,880
-榜单上那个“盲人”是谁？
-就是一个眼睛看不见的人。
-Who's "Blind Man"?
-He was a man who was blind.

342
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:49,920
行吧。
Okay.

343
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:52,320
你以前看过这节目吗？
Have you seen this
show before?

344
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:53,720
我上周正好瞟到了片尾字幕。
I caught the end credits
last week.

345
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:56,160
我本来想着该看看的，结果全给忘了。
I thought I should watch
and I forgot.

346
00:19:56,200 --> 00:20:00,520
主要是他们跟我说：“你能来录节目吗？
我们借你一辆DB9开整个周末。”
Thing is, they said, "Will you
come on? We'll lend you a DB9
for the weekend."

347
00:20:00,560 --> 00:20:01,640
我立马就答应了，DB9也到手了，
And I said yes and
I had the DB9,

348
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:04,440
接着我就把录节目这档子事
忘得一干二净。
then I totally forgot that
I had to do it.

349
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:06,440
你认得他是谁吗？
Do you know who he is?

350
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:07,880
-那辆DB9开着怎么样？
杰里米·克拉克森，我可是纯直男。
-我当然认得他是谁。
-How was the DB9?
Jeremy Clarkson, I'm straight.
-I do know who he is.

351
00:20:07,920 --> 00:20:09,080
我挺喜欢杰里米·克拉克森的。
I like Jeremy Clarkson.

352
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:11,280
行吧，那就好。
真是谢天谢地了。
Well, that's fine.
Thank God for that.

353
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:13,680
你有没有发现，那些成天强调
自己是直男的人，其实根本就不是？
Have you found that people
who say they're straight
rarely are?

354
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:17,040
-他可没少把这挂在嘴边，对吧？
-是啊。[笑]
-He says it a lot,
doesn't he?
-Yeah. [LAUGHING]

355
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:19,400
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

356
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:22,000
我只是想说，你刚才换衣服时
非得当着我们的面，生怕别人看不见。
I'm just saying you made a
big point of getting changed
in front of us earlier.

357
00:20:22,040 --> 00:20:24,160
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

358
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:27,640
而且中途有一次，
他还拿毛巾抽我来着。
And at one point,
he was flicking me
with his towel.

359
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:31,120
-他刚才有那么一会儿看着确实挺兴奋的。
-那可不是他的毛巾。
-He did look aroused
at one point.
-That was not his towel.

360
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:36,360
那分明是某种真菌赘生物吧。
That's some sort of
fungal growth.

361
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:39,080
才没有。我那是又把《壮志凌云》
里洗澡那段戏
看了一遍。
I wasn't. I was watching the
shower scene
from Top Gunagain.

362
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:42,240
你们明明知道的，
我每次上台之前
都得看一遍。
As you well know,
I watch that before
coming out here.

363
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:45,160
-在“出柜”之前？什么鬼？
-[笑声]
-Before coming out? What?
-[LAUGHTER]

364
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:48,320
听说你刚才还在帮他出谋划策，
教他该买什么车呢。
I gather you're giving
him advice
about what car to buy.

365
00:20:48,360 --> 00:20:50,640
我是稍微给了他那么
一丁点儿买车建议。
I gave him a
little bit of advice
about what car to buy.

366
00:20:50,680 --> 00:20:53,040
你自己开的可是辆罗孚75。
我才没有……
You have a Rover 75.
I don't have...

367
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:54,720
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

368
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:57,440
好吧，我现在已经不开罗孚75了。
Well, I don't have a Rover 75
any more.

369
00:20:57,480 --> 00:21:00,720
-那你现在换成什么了？
-我换了辆Mini Cooper。
-What have you got now?
-I've got a Mini Cooper.

370
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:03,360
-所以你这是开倒车了啊。
-[笑声]
-So you've gone backwards.
-[LAUGHTER]

371
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:06,040
开罗孚75哪还能再怎么倒退！
You can't go backwards
from a Rover 75.

372
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:07,720
-你这不是退成了嘛。
-按理说换啥都只能往高处走了。
-You've managed it.
-The only way is up.

373
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:09,560
可你这车比之前那辆还小。
You've got a smaller car
than you had.

374
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:11,840
行了，先别扯你的车了。
Now, just leave your cars
out of it for the moment.

375
00:21:11,880 --> 00:21:14,960
你的买车史简直惨不忍睹，对吧？
Your car history is woeful,
isn't it?

376
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:17,080
我是说，这大概是我们节目史上
最短的一份用车单了。
I mean, I think it's the
shortest we've ever had.

377
00:21:17,120 --> 00:21:19,040
-先是嘉年华1.1……
-呃，是的，
-It went Fiesta 1.1...
-Well, yes,

378
00:21:19,080 --> 00:21:23,760
嘉年华1.1是我拥有的
第一辆车，
差不多是浅蓝色的。
the Fiesta 1.1 was the
first car I owned.
It was sort of pale blue.

379
00:21:23,800 --> 00:21:28,160
后来大学毕业我搬去伦敦，
大概有十年时间
都没买过车，
And then I moved to London
after university and didn't
have a car for about 10 years,

380
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:32,400
-再后来我买了一辆经典老奔驰。
-也就是1966年的……
-then I bought a
classic Mercedes.
-Which is the 1966...

381
00:21:32,440 --> 00:21:33,680
250SE。
250SE.

382
00:21:33,720 --> 00:21:36,000
-那真是一辆极漂亮的车。
-确实很美。
-That's a beautiful car.
-It really is.

383
00:21:36,040 --> 00:21:37,600
你是阿斯顿·马丁的拥趸吗？
Are you an Aston Martin fan?

384
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:40,960
挺喜欢的，但纯粹是因为
我心理年龄特别幼稚，
I am, but only because
I'm a really childish man

385
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,520
我就爱假装自己
是詹姆斯·邦德那种感觉。
and I like the idea of
pretending to be James Bond.

386
00:21:43,560 --> 00:21:45,680
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

387
00:21:45,720 --> 00:21:49,480
-所以你中意的是DB……
-DB5。不过DB6的腿部空间
是不是更大一点？
-So, you're the DB...
-The 5. The 6 has got a bit
more legroom, is that right?

388
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:50,600
没错，
车身稍微长了一截。
That's true,
it's slightly longer.

389
00:21:50,640 --> 00:21:52,280
那我觉得我更适合开DB6。
So I think I could
do with the 6.

390
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:54,720
-你觉得DB4怎么样？
-什么4？
-What do you think about
the 4?
-What 4?

391
00:21:54,760 --> 00:21:57,680
